 ### Ambient Occlusion via SAT
-Uses cuboid shells and inverse-square weighting to approximate spherical occlusion. Chosen when global shading is needed without light position dependency. [S2, unofficial]
+Uses cuboid shells and inverse-square weighting to approximate spherical occlusion. Sets it apart by caching AO independently of light position, incurring zero rendering cost. Choose when global shading without light dependency is needed. [S2, unofficial]
 
 ### Color Bleeding via SAT
-Stores RGB vectors in the SAT alongside extinction. Chosen when inter-reflection color transfer is required. [S2, unofficial]
+Stores RGB vectors in the SAT alongside extinction. Sets it apart by computing color bleeding simultaneously with the extinction SAT at no extra computation cost. Choose when inter-reflection color transfer is required. [S2, unofficial]
 
 ### Directional Soft Shadows via SAT
-Uses cuboid approximation of light cones. Chosen for soft shadows; static lights are cached, dynamic lights are queried per frame. [S1][S2, unofficial]
+Uses cuboid approximation of light cones. Sets it apart by caching static shadow factors once and querying dynamic shadows per frame. Choose for soft shadows with static or dynamic lights. [S1][S2, unofficial]
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** SAT construction is $O(\log N)$ passes per dimension [S2, unofficial]. Rendering is $O(1)$ per sample for static effects (cache lookup) and $O(K)$ for dynamic shadows (K cuboid queries) [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** SAT construction requires $O(\log N)$ passes per dimension [S2, unofficial]. Rendering cost is zero for cached AO/color bleeding and a single texture lookup for static shadows per sample; dynamic shadows require per-frame SAT queries proportional to the number of cuboid samples [S2, unofficial].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** Requires two auxiliary 3D textures (SAT and Light Cache) [S2, unofficial].
